{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1489485-the-reckoning-the-vigil-s-wardens","id":1489485,"title":"The Reckoning: The Vigil's Wardens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-08T08:36:15-07:00","id":1489485,"title":"The Reckoning: The Vigil's Wardens","content":"So I really like the idea of the Reckoning, but I always felt it could use more. So I've made a C&amp;C style write up, very rough. I didn't mention the Reckoning being a fan of collateral damage, because I thought that was so incredibly contradicting as to be insulting to the compact, but I've added other negatives I think will balance them out. Please give feedback<br /> <br /> Students of God's monsters<br /> <br /> In the beginning, there was Adam and Eve. God had made them in Eden, otherwise known as paradise. They were given only one rule, and that was not to eat the fruit of knowledge. A very simple rule, really. But as everyone knows, a Serpent came along, who tricked Eve into eating the fruit, who then seduced Adam into doing the same. And the two lost paradise forever as punishment.<br /> Many cry out at the evil of the Serpent, but the hunters of the Reckoning point out the Serpent was never punished. In fact, it wasn't so much evil as simply following its nature. The fault is entirely on the original man and woman, but at least they submitted to that...<br /> <br /> The Hero's Pride and Hunters Folly<br /> <br /> Heracles, Gilgamesh, even Wise King Solomon. What do these three have in common? They commit great acts while their failures are swept under the rug in the eyes of the masses. Whether it be fits of rage or falling to pagan beliefs, these figures almost always escape retribution. <br /> Then you have the hunters who forget innocent lives only ended due to their needless hunt for a monster. The Reckoning has made it their mission to contain cells that have caused too much collateral damage, and are even willing to kill (this has made them rather unpopular with the more gung-ho of cells). <br /> <br /> So Monsters are off the Hook?:<br /> Not at all. Jesus sent Legion to the pigs, famously enough. The Reckoning hunts monsters who are out of control, or have no rhyme or reason to their atrocities. Whether it be a ravenous Beast or a murderous Slasher, the compact will go out of their way to kill monsters that end truly innocent lives (whatever that definition is to the compact). But for the most part, monsters don't do that. The vampire feeds on a foolish mortal that falls for it, the idiot teenager trespassed on well known monstrous territory, and so on. The Reckoning is simply less likely to lash out at monsters. Unless THEIR territory is crossed...<br /> <br /> Preparing for the Reckoning:<br /> Despite being much more active, at its heart, the compact is still an isolationist web of a cult (a well presented cult, but a cult nonetheless). And how does this look?<br /> First, you have the compounds. Hidden in forests and more recently city outskirts, these locations are heavily fortified, and armed. The Reckoning has 3 missions for these bases; defend from any threat, whether that be Hero or Monster, indoctrinate and train hunters, and observe the outside for signs of Heroes. <br /> To fund these compounds, the compact presents itself as a down to earth organization that participates in humanitarian acts, while also having members well versed in legal practice when it comes to an easy sue.<br /> At high status, being 4 and 5, a hunter can find that he gets a say on what his compound receives. Its a big honor, but also a burden. These are the compacts prize investments, and it's expected they are taken care of before the hunters needs.<br /> <br /> Wings:<br /> The Reckoning is a well organized compact. While their are arguments on what makes a Hero and at what point a monster has gone out of bounds, Wings are in general accord and have official roles in the compact.<br /> <br /> Messengers: firearms (pistols)<br /> Often hunters who've lost loved ones to heroes, Messengers spend much of their time training. Heroes are strong AND agile, so a Messenger trains to keep his distance while also fighting back effectively. They are also considered the judges of the compact, and keep tabs on allied hunters for if they go on the deep end. For their work, they are quite popular back at the compounds<br /> Secret: they don't like to talk about it, but sometimes, messengers forget monsters need to be put down. In fact, some Messengers have made deals with monsters to keep the peace...at the expense of hunters<br /> <br /> Seeders: subterfuge (recruitment)<br /> The public face of the Reckoning, Seeders are practical men and women who realize how crazy they look. Often appearing at locations recently under supernatural harm, Seeders not only recruit, but do charity work to gain connections with charitable organizations and politicians. This makes them extremely important to the compact.<br /> Secret: recently, Seeders have made increasing contact with the hunters of the Long Night. Despite glaring theological differences, a mix of the downplaying Seeders and the accepting Long Night have given rise to a successful partnership. Who knows what will happen when their belief systems finally clash.<br /> <br /> Castlers: crafts (fortifying)<br /> Can't have compounds without Castlers. Perhaps the most extreme of the compact, Castlers build up their compounds just as they build up hunters. They hardly go out, and usually send others to do their shopping. They are very territorial, even regular citizens.<br /> Secret: religious fundamentalism, guns, and isolationism? This all sounds familiar, and Derek himself wants to the Reckoning to distance itself from a certain past group in Waco. The Castlers aren't too happy with the comparison, and especially don't want to change their beloved compounds.<br /> <br /> Sidebar: Who is Derek, really<br /> Well the founder of the compact, of course. As everyone knows, Derek suffered from a conflict between monster and Hero, and since then has cultivated the compact into what it is today.<br /> But why is Derek so knowledgeable about Heroes and in a way, Beasts? What's caused an incredibly sheltered boy to be a man of such wisdom? Perhaps he's just charismatic and nothing more. Then again, Heroes are too. But Derek is too reasonable to be a Hero. Yeah, certainly there's nothing more to Derek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:39:03-07:00","id":1490538,"title":"","content":"Considering how the Reckoning was one of the less interesting compacts, it is cool to see anything which gives them more depth than &quot;half cult which views fear and beasts as divine presence&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T14:15:09-07:00","id":1490543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1489485-the-reckoning-the-vigil-s-wardens?p=1490538#post1490538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how the Reckoning was one of the less interesting compacts, it is cool to see anything which gives them more depth than &amp;quot;half cult which views fear and beasts as divine presence&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. My main goal was to rectify this issue. I want their flaws to be more about their willingness to let monsters do as they please as long as it's not their compounds or causing &quot;earthquakes&quot; of change. And have a sort of victim blaming mindset to them.<br /> <br /> I also want to have the idea that they appear very rational on the outside, but the further in you get, the more its revealed they have, even for Hunter orgs, an exceedingly odd belief system. Not only that, but if Beasts build their legends and Heroes butt in, the Reckoning observes the legend objectively. Until suddenly it's applied to them, and now the monster is a threat.<br /> <br /> I also want to hint that Derek may be an oracle, that the long night and Reckoning COULD merge (likely the long night winning as most Reckoning hunters aren't as deep in their beliefs), and that they have huge emphasis on building their compounds up.<br /> <br /> Do you have any questions or feedback regarding the write up?<br /> <br /> I may try a write up for a conspiracy level promethean Brotherhood, with Hite revealing the overall agenda of the &quot;real work&quot;. But I genuinely think it may appear in the supplement in a couple years<br /> <br /> also I forgot the intro dialogue<br /> <br /> &quot;Calm dow-HEY, I SAID CALM DOWN. Listen kid, I get it. That man walked out famous for killing a monster while your mother layed dead as bait. And no one cared that could've been avoided. I know pass those tears is a need for retribution. But you can't do it alone. Come along with me kid. I know a place that can help you. By time it's done, that bastard on the screen will know what it is to be a piece of fucking bait.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do hope the intro quote also does the job of the Seeder leaving out the religious aspects while implying the monster should've been kept alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}